WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:14.691
Mowgli returned to the cave.

2
00:00:15.852 --> 00:00:18.014
Mother Wolf sensed something was wrong.

3
00:00:18.034 --> 00:00:20.116
"What is it, son?"

4
00:00:21.397 --> 00:00:24.200
Mowgli didn't want to tell her about the other wolves.

5
00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:28.604
"Oh, some bat was chattering about Shere Khan.

6
00:00:29.376 --> 00:00:33.899
He's hunting nearby, so I think I'll hunt near the people's fields tonight."

7
00:00:34.779 --> 00:00:39.122
With that, Mowgli hurried away, racing downward through the bushes.

8
00:00:40.583 --> 00:00:44.125
Near the stream at the bottom of the valley, he heard howls.

9
00:00:48.127 --> 00:00:49.428
The wolves were hunting.

10
00:00:51.549 --> 00:00:52.770
"Spring, Akela!"

11
00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:54.111
a young wolf shouted.

12
00:00:54.131 --> 00:00:56.092
"Show your strength!"

13
00:00:59.952 --> 00:01:02.534
Mowgli heard teeth snapping and then a yelp.

14
00:01:03.635 --> 00:01:06.457
Akela had sprung at something—and missed.

15
00:01:08.398 --> 00:01:10.419
Mowgli raced on toward the village.

16
00:01:15.222 --> 00:01:18.405
Mowgli had never come this close to the village before.

17
00:01:21.287 --> 00:01:24.028
He slipped over to a hut and peered inside.

18
00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:28.992
A red flower glowed along one wall.

19
00:01:30.208 --> 00:01:32.610
He watched a woman get up and blow on it.

20
00:01:33.731 --> 00:01:35.713
Then she fed it some sticks.

21
00:01:38.655 --> 00:01:39.576
Mowgli sighed.

22
00:01:40.397 --> 00:01:42.118
The red flower was dangerous.

23
00:01:42.919 --> 00:01:43.800
What should he do?

24
00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:47.623
He waited through the night.

25
00:01:49.805 --> 00:01:52.927
In the morning he saw a child pick up a pot.

26
00:01:54.789 --> 00:01:57.992
The boy filled it with lumps of the red-hot flower.

27
00:01:59.548 --> 00:02:00.469
Mowgli laughed.

28
00:02:00.489 --> 00:02:05.792
"That small cub can handle the red flower," he thought.

29
00:02:06.853 --> 00:02:07.733
"So can I!"

30
00:02:10.875 --> 00:02:13.277
He ran at the boy and grabbed the pot.

31
00:02:15.138 --> 00:02:17.399
Then he ran deep into the jungle.

32
00:02:19.781 --> 00:02:24.424
After some time he stopped to blow at the red stuff as the woman had done.

33
00:02:28.312 --> 00:02:29.953
"Now it's time to feed it."

34
00:02:30.913 --> 00:02:33.654
He dropped twigs and bark on the red flower.

35
00:02:34.815 --> 00:02:36.235
It quickly bloomed again.

36
00:02:37.936 --> 00:02:38.876
Mowgli grinned.

37
00:02:38.896 --> 00:02:40.297
"I did it!"

38
00:02:42.178 --> 00:02:44.539
Halfway up the hill he met Bagheera.

39
00:02:45.799 --> 00:02:47.180
The panther looked worried.

40
00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.981
"Akela failed at last night's hunt.

41
00:02:50.821 --> 00:02:54.503
The wolves wanted to kill him, but they were looking for you instead."

42
00:02:54.523 --> 00:02:57.044
"I was in the valley.

43
00:02:57.700 --> 00:02:59.342
I am ready to fight now."

44
00:03:00.483 --> 00:03:02.404
Mowgli held up the fire pot.

45
00:03:04.166 --> 00:03:05.086
Bagheera nodded.

46
00:03:05.106 --> 00:03:09.110
"Good." Then he peered more closely at the red flower.

47
00:03:09.130 --> 00:03:11.391
"Are you afraid of that thing?

48
00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:13.873
It's dangerous when it blooms."

49
00:03:15.255 --> 00:03:16.155
Mowgli shrugged.

50
00:03:16.175 --> 00:03:18.237
"I'm not afraid.

51
00:03:18.797 --> 00:03:21.680
In fact, I remember it from long ago.

52
00:03:22.821 --> 00:03:26.444
Before I was a wolf, I rested near the red flower.

53
00:03:27.452 --> 00:03:29.053
It was warm and pleasant."

54
00:03:32.276 --> 00:03:34.957
That night Mowgli headed to the pack council.

55
00:03:36.098 --> 00:03:39.541
He stayed in the back so the wolves wouldn't see the fire pot.

56
00:03:41.562 --> 00:03:43.904
Mowgli gulped when he saw the empty rock.

57
00:03:44.944 --> 00:03:47.846
Akela lay beside it, injured from the hunt.

58
00:03:49.368 --> 00:03:51.989
The pack was removing him as leader!

59
00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:58.153
Shere Khan walked around the rock, young wolves trailing him.

60
00:03:59.554 --> 00:04:03.036
When everyone had gathered, Shere Khan began to speak.

61
00:04:04.477 --> 00:04:06.338
"He has no right to speak here!"

62
00:04:06.778 --> 00:04:09.240
Bagheera whispered furiously to Mowgli.

63
00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:11.841
Mowgli sprang to his feet.

64
00:04:12.322 --> 00:04:15.483
"Why is he—" "Quiet, man cub!"

65
00:04:15.944 --> 00:04:17.164
some wolves yelled.

66
00:04:18.345 --> 00:04:20.406
Akela slowly raised his head.

67
00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:22.828
"I'm weak and old.

68
00:04:23.856 --> 00:04:27.657
Another wolf must fight me to become the pack's new leader."

69
00:04:29.078 --> 00:04:30.818
There was a long silence.

70
00:04:31.898 --> 00:04:33.659
None wanted to fight Akela.

71
00:04:35.239 --> 00:04:39.020
"I want only the man cub," Shere Khan roared.

72
00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:43.942
"Give me the man cub, and I will leave your pack alone."

73
00:04:43.962 --> 00:04:47.123
"Let the tiger take Mowgli!"

74
00:04:47.463 --> 00:04:48.403
a wolf yelled.

75
00:04:48.423 --> 00:04:51.324
"Mowgli is not a wolf!"

76
00:04:52.956 --> 00:04:54.677
Akela lifted his head again.

77
00:04:54.697 --> 00:04:58.658
"Mowgli has eaten our food and slept with us.

78
00:04:59.578 --> 00:05:02.199
He has not broken the law of the jungle.

79
00:05:02.759 --> 00:05:03.699
He's our brother."

80
00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:06.520
"No, he's a man!"

81
00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:08.160
the pack snarled.

82
00:05:09.261 --> 00:05:11.061
Shere Khan's tail flicked.

83
00:05:12.382 --> 00:05:13.882
Bagheera glanced at Mowgli.

84
00:05:14.702 --> 00:05:20.284
"Now!" Mowgli stood upright—showing the fire pot to the pack.

85
00:05:21.824 --> 00:05:24.605
"You've often told me that I am not a wolf.

86
00:05:25.546 --> 00:05:29.307
So I won't call you my sisters and brothers anymore!"

87
00:05:30.267 --> 00:05:32.428
He flung the fire pot on the ground.

88
00:05:33.849 --> 00:05:37.030
Swiftly it bloomed into furious flames.
